                "summary": "AC1 falsified in rest mode: segmentStream places a rest cut inside a bridged dropout (src/recognition/segment.ts:160-164; probe: hand lost 1440-1840 ms inside a rest, segments [0..1640] and [1680..4000], both boundary frames handless). Fix: snap the cut to hand frames (advance cut to the next frame with a hand, end the earlier part at the last hand frame before it) and add a unit test with a dropout inside a rest. All 24 docs table rows reproduce exactly with EVAL_FULL-size options; simulateProfileUnder and seeds unchanged; no threshold changed. Non-blocking: away-mode equality with one-by-one is by construction (withoutEmptyEnds + instant enter/leave make each segment the capture itself), so docs should say the synthetic away rows only check boundary recovery; rest-pause spans include rests so 'said in a pause' cannot fire there; surviving mutants: tri-state null-as-rest, two-hand any-moving rule, open split in rest mode, bridge-limit in movingFrames, gap > vs >=.",
